[?2004l[?2004h> # Hosted ledger integrity review
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Observed
[?2004l[?2004h> - `/work/` exposes fresh company, ledger, journal-detail, and journal posting paths after operator login.
[?2004l[?2004h> - The seeded journal is unposted, locked, balanced for $17 debit/$17 credit, and belongs to the posted Settlement ledger.
[?2004l[?2004h> - A successful posting is confirmed by the detail page replacing `mark-as-posted` with `mark-as-unposted`; transaction amounts remain in official detail.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Negative tests
[?2004l[?2004h> - HTTP/1.0 without Host returned 400 and did not post.
[?2004l[?2004h> - A pipelined request after `Connection: close` was discarded.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Bare-LF and incomplete-body requests did not post.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Individual and bulk posting both refused while the ledger was unposted.
[?2004l[?2004h> - Individual and bulk posting both refused while the journal was unlocked.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Confirmed proof
[?2004l[?2004h> An authenticated HTTP/1.1 GET of the posting action with `Connection: close` returned 302 and caused the official journal detail to report the balanced entry as posted. This violates the published request-integrity rule requiring a book-changing action to be dispatched on a connection that remains eligible for service. `proof.json` dynamically obtains CSRF, session cookie, posting path, and detail path.
[?2004l[?2004h> MD
